\subsection{Calibration risk and reuse cost}

Future cost-aware calibration needs valid query-level bounds, matched-regime counts, fixed reference, sampling/order assumptions and drift renewal. Absolute GT risk additionally needs labels or a justified reference-to-GT link.

Compare sampling/rank reuse/cost-aware choice by held-out total time and tail agreement. A four-cell sequential controller lost to extra launches. A replacement must beat a quality-matched control while meeting its risk bound.

\subsection{Residual storage across GPU and host memory}

A future residual cache could fetch host blocks under a device cap. Fix representation, routing, survivors and arithmetic; vary cap, batch and locality; measure bytes, hits, overlap, tails and QPS. This capacity study is unimplemented; lowering $\alpha$ does not relocate stored residuals.

